import json
from pathlib import Path
base=Path('C:/Users/ADMIN/Desktop/GameAssetFactory/blender/weapons');r=json.loads((base/'weapon_cleanup_report.json').read_text())
lines=['# Weapon geometry cleanup','', 'New revisions created through Blender MCP. Previous working files are preserved. Materials, packed 64x64 atlas, sampling, cyan accents, origins, orientation, marker transforms and overall bounds are unchanged. Only structural geometry was repaired, plus the requested integrated pistol-grip correction.','', '| Asset | Triangles before / after | Blender | GLB | Trigger close-up | Isometric |','|---|---:|---|---|---|---|']
for key,item in r.items():
 b=Path(item['blend']).relative_to(base);g=Path(item['glb']).relative_to(base);pre=b.with_suffix('').as_posix()
 lines.append(f"| {key} | {item['before_triangles']} / {item['after_triangles']} | [Blend]({b.as_posix()}) | [GLB]({g.as_posix()}) | [Close-up]({pre}_trigger_closeup.png) | [Isometric]({pre}_isometric.png) |")
lines+=['', '[Common-scale comparison](weapon_cleanup_comparison.png) / [Comparison Blender scene](weapon_cleanup_comparison.blend).','', '## Findings and repairs','', '- Pistol: 11 unjoined islands and 8 open muzzle-back edges. Old guard had only bottom/front pieces and an unconnected rear end near the grip. Replaced it with one continuous U-section, penetrating both frame attachment regions, then fused and welded it. Added a concealed slide/frame seat and sight feet to eliminate contact-only interfaces. Rebuilt the grip with an integrated upper frame shoulder, clearer angled front strap, and flush shaped heel; removed the separate oversized magazine-like floorplate. Closed the muzzle rear rim and fused the static assembly.','- M4A1: 22 islands and 16 open stock-link/muzzle-back edges. Guard rear/receiver connections were contact-only or gapped. Built a continuous guard; fused grip neck and magazine/magwell junction, stock socket, handguard/receiver transition, barrel/collar interface, rail seat and rear-sight seat. Closed omitted source caps and the muzzle rear rim before union.','- Shotgun: 14 main-mesh islands, 16 open stock-link/muzzle-back edges, and one intentionally separate pump. Rebuilt the guard and fused receiver/grip/stock/rib junctions. Joined the formerly detached fore-end collar to Shotgun_Pump using a bridge, and cut a 2 mm per-side running clearance around the existing guide tube. The pump stays at its original support-hand pivot and is independently movable. No pump animation was authored; travel should be checked against the receiver when animating.','', 'The cleanup uses applied exact unions to replace overlapping interfaces with an exterior surface, followed by vertex welding, degenerate-edge cleanup and normal recalculation. Original exterior faces retain their UV mapping through the unions. Newly exposed connection faces and the requested pistol grip use existing atlas colors. No new materials or texture edits were introduced.','', '## Topology validation','', 'Pistol and rifle each have one connected, closed static body. Shotgun has one connected body plus one connected pump object, the only intentionally separate structure. Triggers were fused into the static body at their upper mount; the trigger cavities remain open visually. Each object has zero boundary/non-manifold edges, zero loose vertices, zero duplicate indexed faces, consistent face winding and positive enclosed volume. Muzzle bores and trigger openings retain manifold walls. No unapplied modifiers remain.','', 'Triangle increases come from real attachment surfaces, intersection topology, completed guard loops and pump clearance walls. Counts remain lightweight: 352 pistol triangles, 760 rifle triangles, 670 shotgun triangles. The pistol is two triangles above the previous approximate 350 target. A UV-preserving planar simplification trial found essentially no removable edges without risking the existing texture appearance.','', '## Export and attachments','', 'All cleaned GLBs have matching measured dimensions, one embedded atlas, one main material and nearest-neighbor sampling. Pistol and M4A1 have one runtime surface; shotgun has two surfaces sharing the material. Marker transforms exactly match the corresponding source assets. Root/main mesh origins stay at the grip center, scale remains one and rotations stay applied. Blender +Y forward / +Z up maps to Godot -Z forward / +Y up. Godot socket and muzzle usage remains as documented in the family README. These exports were not wired into the gameplay project.','', 'Machine-readable results: weapon_cleanup_report.json, geometry_cleanup_before.json, weapon_cleanup_glb_validation.json, weapon_cleanup_preservation_validation.json. Source: cleanup_weapon_geometry.py and build_cleanup_comparison.py. Every preview is RGBA with transparent background.']
(base/'GEOMETRY_CLEANUP.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n')
